{"signature": "{\"model\": \"eleven_multilingual_v2\", \"provider\": \"elevenlabs\", \"settings\": {\"similarity_boost\": 0.85, \"stability\": 0.5, \"style\": 0.0, \"use_speaker_boost\": true}, \"text\": \"Energy cannot be created or destroyed. It can be transferred between stores, but the total energy is conserved. In GCSE Physics, the eight energy stores are chemical, kinetic, gravitational potential, elastic potential, thermal or internal, magnetic, electrostatic and nuclear. Food, fuels and batteries have chemical energy stores. Moving objects have kinetic energy stores. Raised objects have gravitational potential energy stores. A stretched spring or elastic band has an elastic potential energy store. Every object has an internal energy store, which can change when its temperature changes or its state changes. Magnetic and electrostatic stores are associated with interactions involving magnetic and electric fields, while the nuclear store is associated with atomic nuclei.\", \"voice\": \"28e9d9dcea90e5b4\"}", "duration": 54.778776, "words": [["Energy", 0.0], ["cannot", 0.511], ["be", 0.894], ["created", 1.045], ["or", 1.66], ["destroyed.", 1.811], ["It", 2.577], ["can", 2.786], ["be", 3.019], ["transferred", 3.17], ["between", 3.82], ["stores,", 4.249], ["but", 4.818], ["the", 5.004], ["total", 5.143], ["energy", 5.584], ["is", 6.188], ["conserved.", 6.42], ["In", 7.21], ["GCSE", 7.419], ["Physics,", 8.452], ["the", 9.114], ["eight", 9.288], ["energy", 9.625], ["stores", 10.077], ["are", 10.519], ["chemical,", 10.681], ["kinetic,", 11.343], ["gravitational", 12.098], ["potential,", 13.015], ["elastic", 13.735], ["potential,", 14.408], ["thermal", 15.163], ["or", 15.778], ["internal,", 15.999], ["magnetic,", 16.742], ["electrostatic", 17.543], ["and", 18.518], ["nuclear.", 18.739], ["Food,", 20.05], ["fuels", 20.503], ["and", 20.968], ["batteries", 21.177], ["have", 21.769], ["chemical", 22.024], ["energy", 22.651], ["stores.", 23.115], ["Moving", 23.789], ["obje